  "worked_solution": "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220666/assets/6dc32799c53b03cb53d692054cc44910d252367ebf102c53472d4e4d2fe78684.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(0)=\\sqrt{0}=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false since $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is defined for $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III is false, since the graph of $f(x)$ lies in the first quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
